it is likely because the blanket is too hot.\n    *   Sentence structure: \"Pete preferred [X] to [Y], because the [Y] was much hotter.\"\n    *   Why prefer X because Y is hotter? Because you don't like the heat from Y.\n    *   So, Y (blanket) is the \"hotter\" item.\n    *   Therefore, the blank should be \"blanket\".\n\n3.  **Check Options:**\n    *   \"sheet\" or \"blanket\".\n\n4.  **Conclusion:** The blank refers to the item that made the alternative preference logical. The preference is for the sheet. The reason is likely the absence of heat or the presence of heat in the other item. The blank asks for the item that was \"much hotter\". If the sheet was hotter, he wouldn't prefer the sheet. Therefore, the blanket was hotter.\n\n5.  **Output Formatting:**\n    *   Constraint: \"Please provide only the correct option as the answer.\"\n\n6.  **Final Decision:** blanket.\n\n    *   *Self-Correction/Refinement:* Is there any trick? \"Pete preferred to use the sheet to the blanket\" -> Grammar aside, meaning is clear. \"Preferred A to B because B was hotter\". Logic holds. If A (sheet) is cooler, you prefer A over B (blanket) because B (blanket) is hotter.\n    *   Answer: blanket.\n\n7.  **Final Output Generation:** Just the word \"blanket\".",
